course: dictionary
lesson: 1161
title: Context clues: brisket
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A brisket is a cut of meat from the chest of a cow. It is cooked slowly for a long time until it is soft. You may not know the word, but the sentence around it gives clues.
explain: Read this: «Y'all's brisket is drier than the Alamo!» The people are at a barbecue, and brisket is the food being cooked. The Alamo is a famous old building, not something that can be dry, so the speaker is joking. Swap in your meaning: "The meat is very dry" still makes sense.
explain: Other words can sit before brisket, such as beef brisket, smoked brisket and salt beef brisket. The word in front tells you more about the meat. When you are not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: A brisket is a cut of meat from the chest of a cow, cooked slowly until it is soft.
fact: «Brisket» is a noun. You can say a brisket, meaning one piece of meat.
fact: In the USA, especially Texas, brisket is a favourite at barbecues.
fact: Brisket is a Jewish holiday dish, and it is also a slow roast in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: Phrases with brisket include smoked brisket, beef brisket and salt beef brisket.
exercise: What is a brisket? | *A cut of meat from a cow's chest, cooked slowly until soft | A quick fish cake | A fruit that grows on hills | A loud barbecue party
exercise: «Y'all's brisket is drier than the Alamo!» What does the speaker mean? | The brisket is covered in sweet sauce | The Alamo is very dry | The cook has won the prize | *The brisket is very dry, and it is a joke
exercise: Which place is famous for brisket at barbecues? | Canada | *Texas, USA | Japan | Egypt
test: Which word in «smoked brisket» is the noun? | Both are nouns | Smoked | Neither is a noun | *Brisket
test: Which place is NOT given in the lesson as a place where brisket is eaten? | *Mars | UK | USA | Jewish holidays
exam: Mia thinks brisket is a fish because it is cooked at the seaside. What is the best answer? | Brisket is a flower | Brisket is a fish, because fish is cooked at the seaside | Brisket is a kind of bread | *Brisket is meat from a cow's chest, cooked slowly until soft
